            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R3-001",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/skills/role_agents_artifact_test.go:578-590",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "The retirement test only asserts that the 17 retired agents' manifest rows and files are gone. It does not assert that GADU.md and opencode/agents/GADU.md are retired, even though the new apply test's comment names them as retired by this slice. Their rows are still in overlay.manifest as far as the visible diff shows, and the removed test was the only check that pinned them. After this change the GADU rows have no guard in either direction, so an accidental removal or a missed retirement would go undetected.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/skills/role_agents_artifact_test.go:578-590",
                  "engine/installer/agent_deploy_test.go:138-147"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "R3-002",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/installer/agent_deploy_test.go:138-216",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "The new characterization test pins that apply leaves a deployed file in place once its manifest row is gone. The agents the overlay retired therefore stay on existing installs forever, in Claude Code and OpenCode, and nothing in the candidate cleans them up. The test documents this as intended behavior. Whether stale sdd-* and review-* agents remaining beside gentle-ai's own versions is acceptable is left unresolved. If the stale copies shadow or conflict with gentle-ai's agents of the same name, that would be a user-visible effect of this change.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/installer/agent_deploy_test.go:138-216"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Inspected all 20 manifest paths: 17 agent deletions, the two test files and overlay.manifest.",
              "overlay.manifest drops exactly the 17 rows whose files are deleted, so no dangling row points at a missing file.",
              "The new retirement test checks each retired name against manifest rows and against agents/, pi/agents/ and opencode/agents/.",
              "The new apply test exercises a real apply twice, before and after a retirement commit, and asserts the deployed files stay byte for byte.",
              "The minimalism-contract test comment says sdd-tasks and sdd-apply remain in its scope even though their agents are gone. I cannot verify from this candidate that the gate pins that name no longer break."
            ]
          }
        }
